Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "alpha_3_code": filter Singapore 1 km grids (value expected: SGP)  
• "last_updated": choose the most‑recent grid snapshot before 2023‑01‑01  
• "population": population of each 1 km grid cell (to be summed / inspected)  
• "longitude_centroid" / "latitude_centroid": build the point geometry for every grid cell centroid  
• "geog": geography polygon of every grid cell (can be collected → ST_CONVEXHULL)  
• "layer_code": select hospitals (2110 = hospital, 2120 = doctors) in OSM planet layers  
• "geometry": the geometry of every hospital feature  
Conditions that will be useful  
• "alpha_3_code" = 'SGP' (or "country_name" ILIKE '%Singapore%')  
• "last_updated" < '2023‑01‑01'::DATE  
• "layer_code" IN (2110, 2120)  
• ST_INTERSECTS(hospital."geometry", <convex hull of Singapore grids>)  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements, from simple checks to complex spatial joins, all limited to 20 rows.  
